  "interpretation": "Capture-time morphological migratory readiness robustly predicts whether later behavioural migration is expressed. This moves the evidence upstream from final successful escapement to movement initiation itself.",
  "boundary": [
    "The first migration=TRUE row arrival is not treated as onset; the source downstream_migration/time_first_dist_to_use definition is used.",
    "Nine source-specified 2015 classifier-positive tags are treated as expert nonmigrants in the primary analysis; algorithm-only counts are retained as sensitivity.",
    "Missing project migration-table individuals are not recoded as non-initiators.",
    "The result does not establish a stage x landscape-resistance interaction.",
    "Outcome information was inspected during hypothesis development; this is developmental evidence, not preregistered confirmation."
